Root cause:
The root cause of the bug was an off-by-one error introduced in the loop logic within the `network_rx` function in `netfront.c`. The original patch created a break statement that caused the loop to exit prematurely without incrementing the `cons` variable and thereby not processing all responses. This led to the possibility of the same response at the `cons` index being processed multiple times, resulting in unintended behavior. The fix reverts to a clearer control flow and correctly manages the loop's exit condition.
